### miniAODmmmm.cc
    Main version
    All opposite-charge muon pairs with basic kinematic cuts, track quality, and a successful Kalman vertex fit prob  > 0.1.
    Invariant mass in [2.6, 3.6] GeV.
    Valid dimuon candidate with lowest vertexing probability marked with isBestCandidate = true
    Other candidates are also kept (Muons are not reused)
    
    Optionally enables the eventTime for collecting data for emittance scan study.


### miniAODmmmm_Pixelhits.cc
    Collects hit locations in the Pixel detector.
    Identifies the four BPIX layers separately and FPIX hits


### miniAODmmmm_binned.cc - not used
    This code builds a J/ψ mass histogram in fixed bins, separately for each (Run, LumiBlock).
    Mass range is split into nBins = 100 equal-width bins.
    For each mass bin it increments the value of the binkey which is (Run,LumiBlock)

        binCountsMap[(Run,LumiBlock)][bin]++

    For each key it writes one TTree entry containing:

    Run
    LumiBlock
    binCounts = vector of length 100 (the mass-bin counts for that Run–LS)
    So: each tree row is one lumisection, and binCounts[i] is the number of selected dimuon candidates.


